{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788971490,"nonce":"mfnOvRzGLR6Qj6/Tlr4I23AbfNo=","title":"rwa journal does not clear the unread-journal gate — the documented read is the wrong one","message":"`rwa journal` reads `journal/\u003csid\u003e.ndjson` off disk and never calls the `journal` VERB, so the mod's read watermark never moves. An agent following `rwa --help` will be refused `unread-journal` forever while believing it has read the journal.\n\nThis is the exact shape of the wedge that burned run m1-20260901 — sixty consecutive advances, zero in-game ticks, refused `unread-journal` while `journal` was being called every turn (`f08dfc4`, and the run contract's standing rule 5 is written about it).\n\n## Reproduced, openrun-20260909, day 1\n\n    $ rwa journal --since 0 --limit 100      # returns all 39 rows, prints them\n    $ rwa advance --ticks 400\n      REFUSED unread-journal\n      \"39 event(s) ... unread=39 unread_total=39 read_watermark=0 advance_end_seq=39\"\n\nWatermark still 0 after a full successful read. Then:\n\n    $ rwa send journal --since_seq 0 --limit 100\n      read_watermark: 39   unread_after: 0\n    $ rwa advance --ticks 400        # runs\n\nTwo advances were burned before the cause was found. The refusal detail even says *Fix: `journal {since_seq:0}`* — which is the verb call, but the client subcommand of the same name is what a reader reaches for, and its flag is spelled `--since`, not `--since_seq`.\n\n## Why it is worse than a papercut\n\n- `rwa --help` lists `rwa journal [--since N] ...` as the journal reader with no hint that it is file-side.\n- The failure is silent and self-consistent: the rows come back, they are correct, they are complete. Nothing in the client's output says the watermark did not move.\n- The gate it fails to clear is the one that stops the clock. The observed failure mode is an agent that reads, is refused, reads again, is refused, and never moves — with no tick advancing and no error that names the cause.\n- `rwa send journal` works and is undiscoverable from the help text.\n\n## Fixes, any of which closes it\n\n- Make the `rwa journal` subcommand call the verb by default (file-side read behind an explicit `--offline`/`--file` flag). This is the fix that matches what a reader expects.\n- Or, if the file-side read must stay the default, have it print a one-line warning naming `rwa send journal` whenever the mod's watermark is behind the rows it just printed — it can see `status` to know.\n- Either way `--since` and `--since_seq` should not be two different spellings for the same idea across the two paths.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- After the documented journal read, `advance` is not refused with `unread-journal`.\n- `rwa --help`'s journal line states which side of the bridge it reads, if a file-side mode survives.\n- A regression check: read the journal by the documented route, then advance — no refusal. Then read it by the offline route (if kept) and confirm the warning names the verb call.","files":null}]}